LATENT DISPATCH
Mon Sep 14 · 5 items · ~5 min

FERRITE-70B: THE FULL TABLE
We ran it against eleven models on six task families. Summary: best open model on extraction (94.1 field accuracy vs. 91.3 for the next open model), tool selection at 95%, reasoning in the middle of the pack. At the hosted price Kestrel announced ($0.60 / $1.80 per million), it is the cheapest model that clears our "production-ready for structured work" bar. Table, prompts, and raw outputs: https://latentdispatch.ai/p/ferrite-70b-table

PELAGIC DEPRECATES 2.0, 12 MONTHS' NOTICE
True to the policy they published two weeks ago. 2.0 shuts off September 2027; 2.5 is a drop-in for most use, but the reasoning-token behavior differs, so re-run your cost model before migrating.

PROMPT INJECTION IS STILL A THING
A security researcher demonstrated an injection through a vendor invoice PDF: instructions hidden in white text told an accounts-payable agent to approve the invoice and email a confirmation. The agent did. Two lessons: treat every document as untrusted content, and never let a model's output trigger an irreversible action without a human or a hard rule in between. https://latentdispatch.ai/p/invoice-injection

OSTRAVA LABS SIGNS WITH ARGENT
Their document model will be hosted on Argent's EU and US regions from October. Pricing to follow.

SHORT TAKES
· Lodestone-R2 gets a 15% price cut. Reasoning is following the curve, slowly.
· Brindle's replay format gets adopted by Larkspur. Interop wins.
· Sable-3 Mini is now on every major provider.

